# Local `act` defaults for reproducing _build-and-test.yml off a runner
# (soldr#3039 / soldr#3041). act reads this file and keeps only lines that
# start with `-`, splitting each on the FIRST whitespace into flag + value --
# so the value must not be quoted here, or the quotes reach docker verbatim.
#
# `soldr-act-24.04:local` is NOT on a registry -- build it once per machine:
#
#   docker build -t soldr-act-24.04:local ci/act-runner
#
# It is `catthehacker/ubuntu:act-24.04` plus rustup, which that minimal image
# omits and GitHub's ubuntu-24.04 runner ships preinstalled; without it the
# "Install rustup 1.95.0" step dies with `rustup: command not found`.
#
# The job is gated on `github.ref_name == 'main' || github.event_name ==
# 'pull_request'`, so a bare `act` (a `push` on a feature branch) silently
# skips it. Drive it as a pull_request with an event payload:
#
#   act pull_request -e ci/act-runner/pull-request-event.json \
#     -W .github/workflows/ci.yml -j build-linux-x64 --pull=false \
#     -s GITHUB_TOKEN="$(gh auth token)"
-P ubuntu-24.04=soldr-act-24.04:local
--container-options --memory=32g --cpus=8
--cache-server-path .act-cache
--artifact-server-path .act-artifacts
